<p style=3D'margin:0in;margin-left:.375in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.=
0pt'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0</span>* You (the user) want to send a mes=
sage. This
is like the Application Layer.</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;margin-left:.375in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.=
0pt'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0</span>* You write <span style=3D'font-wei=
ght:bold;
color:#0070C0'>your message on a piece of paper</span>. This is like the <s=
pan
style=3D'font-weight:bold;color:#C00000'>HTTP data</span> (your web request=
, like
&quot;get me this webpage&quot;).</p>

<p style=3D'margin:0in;margin-left:.375in;font-family:Calibri;font-size:11.=
0pt'><span
style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>=C2=A0</span>* You<span style=3D'font-weight:bol=
d;color:#0070C0'>
put the message into an envelope</span>. This envelope is like the<span
style=3D'font-weight:bold;color:#C00000'> TCP header and data.</span> TCP e=
nsures
the message reaches the right person and in the correct order. It adds
